{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"00b319d7ae838cc3d3bba24368ea64c217cac19ea4aca8fe59d45eca2dc63c2f","digest":{"component_or_area":"ticket close path and compaction","key_entities":["src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py","_compact_on_close","_compact_locked",".ticket-write.lock.d","src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py","tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_compact_on_close_skip_7084.py","tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_does_not_compact_barbet.py","rebar compact"],"problem_keywords":["write lock hold","compaction","close","performance degradation","blocking","ticket store"],"propositions":["closing a ticket invokes _compact_on_close, which holds the store write lock for minutes (measured up to 13m53s) while folding events, reducing/retiring sources, and committing to git","the store lock hold is unbounded; nested git operations attempt their own flocks with separate budgets that stack inside the held lock, causing concurrent agents to exhaust acquire budgets and lose writes","compaction on close is optional housekeeping for correctness but causes performance and blocking issues; removing the trigger restores lock holds to seconds while preserving manual `rebar compact <id>` and enabling out-of-band compaction","a close with no compaction trigger produces no SNAPSHOT, no retired sources, and no COMPACT commit, leaving events unfolded but correct and replayed normally by the reducer"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787317992795181001,"uuid":"81a99487-3fed-43c7-87ab-364ce9e63ed5"}